      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.02,
          "en": "Now, with that, we're almost done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.02,
          "end": 6.84,
          "en": "but there's one additional thing I wanna do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.84,
          "end": 8.496,
          "en": "related to providers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.496,
          "end": 10.41,
          "en": "Because I mentioned before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.41,
          "end": 12.96,
          "en": "that we're now also going to build a provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.96,
          "end": 15.72,
          "en": "that depends on other providers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.72,
          "end": 19.5,
          "en": "And I'll do this to get this logic here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.5,
          "end": 20.61,
          "en": "which we currently have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.61,
          "end": 24.27,
          "en": "in the build method of my tab screen state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.27,
          "end": 28.263,
          "en": "to get this logic here out of this build method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.22,
          "end": 32.16,
          "en": "Instead, I wanna move this logic here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.16,
          "end": 35.703,
          "en": "essentially into my filters_provider file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.9,
          "end": 40.26,
          "en": "And I'll do this by adding another provider here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.26,
          "end": 41.093,
          "en": "because of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.093,
          "end": 44.25,
          "en": "you can add multiple providers to the same file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.25,
          "end": 47.97,
          "en": "I just typically like to spread them across multiple files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.97,
          "end": 50.04,
          "en": "to keep things separated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.04,
          "end": 53.82,
          "en": "but if multiple providers are closely related to each other,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.82,
          "end": 57.3,
          "en": "it also makes sense to put them into the same file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 57.3,
          "end": 60.48,
          "en": "And that's exactly what is the case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.48,
          "end": 62.73,
          "en": "Because here, I'll add a new provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.73,
          "end": 64.63,
          "en": "which I'll name filteredMealsProvider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.68,
          "end": 69.36,
          "en": "And as the name suggests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.36,
          "end": 71.34,
          "en": "here I wanna create a provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.34,
          "end": 74.73,
          "en": "which returns a list of filtered meals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.73,
          "end": 79.59,
          "en": "So, in the end, a provider that contains this logic here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.59,
          "end": 82.68,
          "en": "And therefore I can already cut this logic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.68,
          "end": 86.55,
          "en": "and bring it over to filters_provider.dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.55,
          "end": 90.69,
          "en": "Because here, this provider will now be a simple provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.69,
          "end": 93,
          "en": "not a StateNotifierProvider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93,
          "end": 96.53999999999999,
          "en": "because I won't create a new FiltersNotifier class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.53999999999999,
          "end": 98.28,
          "en": "or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.28,
          "end": 102.39,
          "en": "But instead, a standard provider, which gets this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.39,
          "end": 104.43,
          "en": "which receives a ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.43,
          "end": 106.11,
          "en": "where in this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.11,
          "end": 109.17,
          "en": "I now paste in that code, which I copied,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.17,
          "end": 112.97999999999999,
          "en": "where I then want to return this filtered list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.97999999999999,
          "end": 115.53,
          "en": "But of course, now meals isn't available here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.53,
          "end": 118.02000000000001,
          "en": "and neither is activeFilters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.31,
          "end": 122.49,
          "en": "So, in the end, now this filteredMealsProvider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.49,
          "end": 125.91,
          "en": "must depend on both the filtersProvider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.91,
          "end": 127.74,
          "en": "which of course may change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.74,
          "end": 130.833,
          "en": "because the filters that have been set can be changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.67,
          "end": 134.64,
          "en": "But we also must depend on the meals_provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.64,
          "end": 136.44,
          "en": "which indeed will never change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.44,
          "end": 140.659,
          "en": "but which in theory could also provide dynamic data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.659,
          "end": 143.82,
          "en": "So, how can we depend on these providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143.82,
          "end": 145.68,
          "en": "inside of this provider?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.68,
          "end": 148.339,
          "en": "Well, by using this ref argument here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.339,
          "end": 152.22,
          "en": "Up to this point, whenever we created a provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.22,
          "end": 154.62,
          "en": "we never used this ref argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.62,
          "end": 156.827,
          "en": "We only did that in our widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.827,
          "end": 159.75,
          "en": "But the ref argument we get here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.75,
          "end": 161.85,
          "en": "automatically by Riverpod,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.85,
          "end": 164.16,
          "en": "is in the end, the same ref argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.16,
          "end": 167.91,
          "en": "the same ref object we can use in our widgets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.91,
          "end": 171.51,
          "en": "It allows us to read or watch providers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.51,
          "end": 174.69,
          "en": "And that's exactly what I want do here now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.69,
          "end": 178.07999999999998,
          "en": "Inside of this function, I wanna set up a watcher",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.07999999999998,
          "end": 180.967,
          "en": "to my mealsProvider, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.967,
          "end": 185.88,
          "en": "Now, for that, we must import this mealsProvider.dart file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.88,
          "end": 187.593,
          "en": "from the provider's folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.52,
          "end": 191.319,
          "en": "But with it imported, we can set up a watcher.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.319,
          "end": 193.92,
          "en": "And if you do set up a watcher here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.92,
          "end": 196.23,
          "en": "the riverpod package will make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.23,
          "end": 199.2,
          "en": "that this function here gets re executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.2,
          "end": 203.57999999999998,
          "en": "whenever the watched value changes, so that in the end here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 203.57999999999998,
          "end": 206.61,
          "en": "you can then return an updated data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 206.61,
          "end": 208.68,
          "en": "and any widgets that would be listening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 208.68,
          "end": 211.92000000000002,
          "en": "to this provider would then also be updated if one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 211.92000000000002,
          "end": 215.04,
          "en": "of the dependencies of that provider would update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 215.04,
          "end": 218.133,
          "en": "All of that would happen automatically behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.63,
          "end": 221.88,
          "en": "So with that here I get my meals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.88,
          "end": 225.09,
          "en": "and now we can do the same for the active filters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.09,
          "end": 227.28,
          "en": "Here I can get my active filters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.28,
          "end": 231.153,
          "en": "by watching my filters provider like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 232.11,
          "end": 234.96,
          "en": "So this provider here, I'm watching this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 234.96,
          "end": 238.74,
          "en": "so whatever this changes, this function is re executed and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 238.74,
          "end": 241.233,
          "en": "therefore the filtered meals are recalculated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 242.19,
          "end": 245.16,
          "en": "Well and now with this new provider added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 245.16,
          "end": 247.98,
          "en": "a provider which now depends on other providers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 247.98,
          "end": 251.373,
          "en": "which as you see is super easy to implement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 251.373,
          "end": 254.52,
          "en": "But with this provider added, we can now go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 254.52,
          "end": 256.59,
          "en": "to the tabs.dart file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 256.59,
          "end": 259.8,
          "en": "and there, instead of manually getting the meals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 259.8,
          "end": 263.73,
          "en": "and the filtersprovider, we now can get the available meals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 263.73,
          "end": 266.94,
          "en": "by using ref.watch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.94,
          "end": 270.84,
          "en": "And then here, I wanna watch my filteredMealsProvider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 270.84,
          "end": 275.4,
          "en": "So this new provider I just added, which returns this list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 275.4,
          "end": 280.02,
          "en": "of meals, this list of filtered meals to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 280.02,
          "end": 283.08,
          "en": "And with that, we moved this filtering logic out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 283.08,
          "end": 284.38,
          "en": "of this build method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 285.65999999999997,
          "end": 287.4,
          "en": "This now also means that we can get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 287.4,
          "end": 289.44,
          "en": "of this meals provider import here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 289.44,
          "end": 291.69,
          "en": "because we're not using anything from this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.69,
          "end": 293.412,
          "en": "file here anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 293.412,
          "end": 296.22,
          "en": "But with all that, if we now save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 296.22,
          "end": 299.25,
          "en": "and restart the app, you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 299.25,
          "end": 304.23,
          "en": "that if you set some filters here, this still works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 304.23,
          "end": 307.92,
          "en": "and certain values are still filtered out whilst other meals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 307.92,
          "end": 310.17,
          "en": "are still visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 310.17,
          "end": 312.66,
          "en": "So this app still works as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 312.66,
          "end": 314.97,
          "en": "but now we're also using a provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 314.97,
          "end": 317.133,
